          "statement": "Prove the construction independent of the affine cover and compatible with proper equivariant maps with proper fixed loci; when p itself is proper it agrees with genuine proper pushforward. Use actual self-intersection and Thom purity to compute p_*loc(\u03b1 cap[X])=sumF pF*((i*\u03b1/eT\u03bdF) cap[F]). For finite F this is the finite reciprocal Euler sum, with degree shifts and empty fixed set correct. The result applies to the separately proved smooth separated stable ADHM quotient and its finite invariant word-slice atlas/partition fixed locus, but those ADHM-specific facts are consumed later in old12 to avoid a page cycle.",
