        {
          "id": "thm-qftx-taubes-arbitrary-divisor-plane-vortex",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Planar critical vortices for arbitrary finite divisors",
          "statement": "For every effective finite divisor D=sum m_j[z_j] on R2, of total degree N>=0, and kappa=2e\u00b2xi>0, prove unique distributional h satisfying Delta h+kappa(1-exp h)=4pi sum m_j delta_zj, h->0, and h-2m_j log|z-zj| smooth near each centre. If N>0, prove h<0 off the divisor; for empty D prove h=0 and the flat constant vacuum. Prove smooth gauge reconstruction, finite energy, flux 2pi N, and exponential decay of h and its derivatives (any rate strictly below sqrt(kappa)), hence of gauge-invariant curvature/covariant gradients; state field decay in a canonical exterior gauge rather than falsely requiring the raw polynomial phase to decay exponentially. All arbitrary centres/multiplicities retained; negative winding by reflection/conjugation.",
