          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "proof_obligation": " Exhaust disks using the previous explicit barriers and fixed singular subtraction; obtain smooth limits using the exact n=2 elliptic estimates and Ascoli. For strict negativity, if w=-h>=0 and Delta w<=kappa w, then w(x)cos(sqrt(kappa)t) is nonnegative superharmonic on a narrow 3D slab; the classical subharmonic strong maximum principle applied to its negative propagates any zero, contradicting logarithmic singularities. For exterior decay use C exp(-alpha(r-R)), alpha<sqrt(kappa), and the classical comparison for Delta-c with alpha\u00b2<c<kappa; no special-function supplier is required. Prove derivatives decay by local estimates before asserting finite energy. Uniqueness follows from the weak maximum principle on expanding disks applied to the smooth difference after logarithmic cancellation. Treat empty divisor separately: h=0, flat connection and constant scalar, without a false strict-negativity assertion. Polynomial-phase reconstruction has algebraic phase tails for displaced centres; gauge-invariant h/B/Dq decay exponentially, and a smooth degree-zero exterior gauge cleanup produces canonical field tails.",
