+# Supplemental Alpha prerequisite drift review — append 1
+
+### qftx-sobolev-gauge-orbit-geometry
+
+The order-958.25 A-page row has five item declarations. Their actual external item suppliers are covered by the declared page closure: gauge geometry and principal-connection/gauge-group definitions; Sobolev multiplication and embedding; Banach inverse/implicit function theorems; unitary Schur theory and ODE dependence; compact elliptic/Hodge theory and bounded-inverse perturbation. The hypotheses fix compact connected oriented boundaryless Riemannian $M$ of dimension three or four, an $SU(N)$ bundle, integer $k>d/2+1$, and the reduced central quotient. The scaffold explicitly requires local proofs of Sobolev gauge calculus, properness, the rough-coefficient Green inverse and smooth-topology compatibility; it does not incorrectly treat the imported smooth-coefficient Green result as sufficient. No missing prerequisite page was found.
+
+VERDICT: no-drift
+
+### qftx-irreducible-connection-topology
+
+The order-958.5 row declares the Sobolev gauge-geometry page, compactness, higher homotopy, Sard/transversality, Whitney approximation and parameter-dependent ODE pages used by its three item declarations. The claims are restricted to smooth principal $SU(N)$ bundles over $S^3$ or $S^4$ and use irreducibility of the holonomy representation, not full holonomy. The scaffold supplies a finite-loop and finite-dimensional incidence/Sard route with relative smoothing; Singer’s cited theorem is an outline, not a substitute supplier. The actual imported supplier pages needed for that route lie in the declared closure. No missing prerequisite page was found.
+
+VERDICT: no-drift
+
+### qftx-gauge-group-sphere-homotopy
+
+The order-958.75 row originally declared the sphere-fibration, homotopy, Freudenthal, Whitney and Sobolev pages. The source-backed construction of `lem-qftx-low-unitary-homotopy-inputs` also uses the Hopf-bundle calculation of $\pi_3(S^2)$, the Hopf-cone coefficient, cellular and pair cohomology, the Künneth ring calculation, and Steenrod-square naturality/top-square and Adem relations to prove the needed finite $\pi_4(S^3)$ and nonzero $\pi_5(S^3)$. The exact imported supplier pins and homes are recorded in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gauge-low-homotopy-sources/reading-and-context.json`; its proof dossier reconstructs the relevant argument and does not rely on the James or EHP computations. Hatcher’s author-hosted appendices give the complete three-cell contradiction in Proposition 4L.11 (printed pp. 498–499): the two $Sq^2$ maps are isomorphisms, contradicting $Sq^2Sq^2=Sq^3Sq^1$ and the vanishing of $Sq^1$ in the intervening degree ([source](https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~Hatcher/AT/ATch4.4.pdf)).
+
+Added the nine missing existing supplier-page edges to this A row: `classification-of-covering-spaces`, `the-fundamental-group-of-the-circle`, `chern-and-pontryagin-classes-by-splitting-and-complexification`, `bocksteins-steenrod-squares-and-cohomology-operations`, `cup-cap-cross-products-and-cohomology-rings`, `relative-homology-excision-and-mayer-vietoris`, `cw-complexes-and-cellular-homology`, `singular-cohomology-and-coefficient-theorems`, and `obstruction-theory-postnikov-towers-and-classifying-spaces`. The page order remains 958.75 and every added imported prerequisite is earlier. No item declaration or claim scope was changed. The required plan validator passed after this correction.
+
+VERDICT: drift-applied
+
+### qftx-adhm-linear-data-and-framed-monads
+
+The order-967.2 A row has six item declarations. Direct item-supplier homes, including quotient-manifold and tangent results, matrix spectral/implicit-function results, projective cohomology and Serre duality, hypercohomology, affine invariant theory and the finite-type scheme results, are all in the declared 15-page requirement closure. Their hypotheses retain $N\ge1$, $k\ge0$, the explicit $GL(V)$ action, word stability/costability, the separate positive-FI and zero-FI levels, and the stated framing-torus convention. GAGA, family/base-change, and monad reconstruction remain complete local proof obligations rather than assumed dictionary results. No missing prerequisite page was found.
+
+VERDICT: no-drift
+
+### qftx-adhm-zero-fi-asd-correspondence
+
+The order-967.3 row’s five item declarations have their ADHM linear-data, instanton-number, Chern–Weil, projective cohomology/duality and hypercohomology supplier homes in the declared page closure. The scope distinguishes regular zero-FI data from positive-FI stable data and fixes the oriented round $S^4$, framing, real structure and $k=-q_N$ normalization. The Penrose–Ward, coupled vanishing/monad reconstruction and charge-normalization arguments are explicitly still to be proved locally; the plan does not present Donaldson’s roadmap or an ordinary index formula as a complete dictionary proof. These obligations do not expose an additional prerequisite page absent from the declared closure. No missing prerequisite page was found.
+
+VERDICT: no-drift
+
+### qftx-noncompact-equivariant-borel-moore-localization
+
+The order-967.4 row’s six item declarations use the declared Borel–Moore/six-functor, equivariant constructible, torus-cohomology, Euler/Thom, fixed-point and exact-localization supplier pages. Their hypotheses specify a separated finite-type complex variety with a finite invariant affine atlas, rational torus coefficients and, for the localized trace, a proper fixed locus. The general concentration/localization result is proved independently of the ADHM application, which remains a downstream consumer; this avoids a prerequisite cycle. No missing prerequisite page was found.
+
+VERDICT: no-drift
+
+### qftx-abelian-higgs-vortex-existence-mathematics
+
+The order-967.5 row’s five item declarations have the required Sobolev, Dirichlet resolver, weak maximum principle, $W^{2,p}$/Schauder regularity, extension, Ascoli, strong comparison, Stokes and Fubini suppliers in the declared 11-page closure. The scope is a purely mathematical critical Abelian–Higgs problem on $\mathbb R^2$, including arbitrary finite divisors and the empty divisor; the proof design supplies disk barriers and exhaustion instead of relying on an incomplete citation. Tong’s cited pages give model and square-completion context, while the Taubes record is metadata only and explicitly does not claim full-text reading. No missing prerequisite page was found.
+
+VERDICT: no-drift
